I would be surprised to meet an arch-lich there.

If your level is not too high, they are guaranteed to not be higher than 
demi-lich...  So it depends on how fast you get to the castle.  Also, as 
I said, you might be able to demote one master lich without losing too 
much armor.  (Just take the kit armor off on the castle level...)

Yes, we were discussing -- among other things -- the utility of the 
castle wand to obtain magic resistance in the first place.  Why should 
this prevent me from remarking that this is a rare situation for me?


>> Again, if they are not master liches or higher, you may be able to 
>> keep them off bay with ranged weapons or wands.  Or you lose one piece 
>> of armor, before killing them.

> So you are just talking about a special case that the 2-3 liches are of
> the easy kind. A good tactics should consider that NH reality differs.

It does not, because they are of the easy kind, if you make sure that 
your level is not too high when reaching the castle.  On the other hand, 
we are talking about a rare case here.  This means that you may need to 
do best with what you have.  No *very* good strategy may be available to 
you...


> If you don't have MR a tougher kind of lich will immediately teleport to
> the stairs and destroy your speed boots or so.  Would you neglect that?
> Without MR I would either immediately leave the place or genocide the
> liches.

I would immediately move upstairs on noting that I am on the castle 
level.  (The master lich will not normally arrive on your first turn.) 
Then I would take off the speed boots and any armor that is not 
disposable.  I would usually carry some spare disposable armor in a bag. 
Next I would go down and try to kill the master lich.  Of course, I 
would also consider the two options you give :-).  If I have a scroll of 
genocide, then I might get rid of master liches even before entering the 
castle level.

> But why are you talking just about "one piece" of armor?  Have you any
> means against liches that guarantees their quick death before they cast
> another spell?

Cockatrice corpses :-) ...  No, but I don't think they will take off a 
piece in each turn.  This might happen, and then I would be in trouble. 
  (But not having MR by the castle is trouble already.)  But usually, 
with a well-enchanted artifact weapon (without that *and* without MR, I 
would not go down to the castle) the fight lasts a few turns only.  If 
you are naked by then with the exception of the armor you took off, well 
you know what to wish for later...

Of course, you should make sure to be able to kill a master lich fast, 
since the touch of death is much more of a problem than your armor.  So 
go down only if you have a cockatrice corpse handy...

Anyway, *if* I have to go to the castle to get magic resistance, I am 
usually sufficiently low-level, too (12 - 15).  I don't know at what 
level master liches start to appear, but it happens more often to me 
than not that the castle does not contain one.
